stateDiagram-v2
    %% SP7 - Condition of an installed PC or monitor (RoomEquipment.condition, A-07, DD-CLS-01, DD-ISS-01)
    state "Under Repair" as UnderRepair
    state "Out of Service" as OutOfService

    [*] --> Installed : item installed in room<br/>[Desktop or Monitor, not installed elsewhere]

    state Installed {
        [*] --> Working
        Working --> Faulty : Hardware issue reported (auto)<br/>or setCondition(Faulty)
        Faulty --> UnderRepair : linked issue → In Progress (auto)
        UnderRepair --> Working : linked issue resolved<br/>[no other unresolved issue on item]
        UnderRepair --> OutOfService : linked issue resolved with "Out of Service"<br/>[no other unresolved issue on item]
        Faulty --> OutOfService : setCondition(Out of Service)
        OutOfService --> UnderRepair : setCondition(Under Repair)
        Working --> Missing : room check: item missing
        Missing --> Working : item found
    }

    Installed --> Removed : removeEquipment() or moveEquipment(target)<br/>or item retired on Assets page<br/>/ removedAt = now
    Removed --> [*]

    note right of Installed
        Any manual change uses setCondition(new, reason):
        reason is required, same value gives "No change".
        Every change is audit-logged (old, new, reason, user).
        A move closes this record and opens a new one
        in the target room with the same condition.
    end note
